      "id": "m34",
      "question": "How do I use one uploaded file with both OpenAI and Anthropic?",
      "inScope": true,
      "askedAt": "2026-09-29T22:00:48.900Z",
      "classification": "answered-with-citations",
      "answer": "Upload the file separately to OpenAI and Anthropic using `uploadFile`, then merge the returned `providerReference` objects. [1: \"you need to upload the file to both providers and merge the references\"] For example, pass `openai.files()` and `anthropic.files()` as the `api` values, along with the same file data and filename. [1: \"uploadFile({\\n  api: openai.files(),\\n  data: imageBytes,\\n  filename: 'photo.png',\"] [1: \"api: anthropic.files(),\\n  data: imageBytes,\\n  filename: 'photo.png',\"]\n\nMerge them with `{ ...openaiResult.providerReference, ...anthropicResult.providerReference }`. [1: \"const mergedReference = {\\n  ...openaiResult.providerReference,\\n  ...anthropicResult.providerReference,\"] You can then use that merged reference in messages with either provider; each one will find its own file ID. [1: \"each provider will find its own file ID\"]",
      "citations": [
