    {
      "id": "m36",
      "question": "How do I upload a custom skill to a provider?",
      "inScope": true,
      "askedAt": "2026-09-29T22:00:54.892Z",
      "classification": "answered-with-citations",
      "answer": "Call `uploadSkill` with the provider’s skills API, the skill files (each with a relative `path` and `content`), and optionally a `displayTitle`. It returns a `providerReference` you can pass to later inference calls. [1: \"function to upload custom skills to a provider and get back a `ProviderReference`\"]\n\nFor example, use `api: anthropic.skills()` or `api: openai.skills()`; those providers support skill uploads. [2: \"Anthropic | `anthropic.skills()` | OpenAI    | `openai.skills()`\"] You can also pass the provider instance directly, such as `api: anthropic`, as shorthand. [1: \"you can pass a provider instance directly to `api` instead of calling `.skills()` explicitly\"]\n\nThe skill files can contain bytes (`Uint8Array`) or base64-encoded strings. [4: \"File content can be provided as a `Uint8Array` (e.g. from `fs.readFileSync`) or as a base64-encoded string\"]",
