    {
      "id": "m40",
      "question": "What happens if one of my lifecycle callbacks throws?",
      "inScope": true,
      "askedAt": "2026-09-29T22:01:04.620Z",
      "classification": "answered-with-citations",
      "answer": "If a lifecycle callback throws, the error is caught internally and the AI SDK call continues; it does not break the generation flow. [4: \"If a callback throws, the error is caught internally and the AI SDK call continues.\"] For tool execution callbacks, thrown errors are likewise silently caught and do not break generation. [3: \"Errors thrown inside these callbacks are silently caught and do not break the generation flow.\"]",
